==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|upland}}, equal to {{prefix|up|land|lang=en}}. Compare {{m|en|inland}}, {{m|enm|midland}}, {{m|en|outland}}, etc.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of, relating to, or situated in the uplands.
#* Milton
#*: Sometimes, with secure delight / The '''upland''' hamlets will invite.
#* Chapman
#*: the race of '''upland''' giants

===Derived terms===
* {{l|en|uplander}}
* {{l|en|uplandish}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|upland moccasin}}
* {{l|en|upland sandpiper}}
* {{l|en|upland sumach}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[area]] in the [[interior]] of a [[country]] with a [[generally]] [[higher]] [[elevation]]; often [[hilly]], but not generally [[mountainous]] (compare [[highland]]s).

====Hypernyms====
